# portal/.htaccess
#
# VULN NOTES - this file is intentionally minimal:
#
# #6  Directory Listing Enabled
#     No "Options -Indexes" directive - if a directory has no index.php,
#     Apache will list its contents (e.g. try /portal/uploads/profile_photos/).
#
# #1/#17/#18/#19  Missing security headers
#     No Header directives for Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options,
#     X-Content-Type-Options, Strict-Transport-Security, Referrer-Policy.
#     A hardened version of this file would add, e.g.:
#         Header set X-Frame-Options "DENY"
#         Header set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
#         Header set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'"
#         Header set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains"
#     None of that is present here on purpose.
#
# #15 Missing HTTPS Enforcement
#     No RewriteEngine/RewriteCond redirecting http:// to https://.
#
# #14 (supporting) uploads/ has no handler restriction here either -
#     a hardened version would disable PHP execution inside uploads/:
#         <Directory "uploads">
#             php_flag engine off
#         </Directory>
#     Intentionally omitted - see VULNERABILITIES.md #14.
